w relationships that i've  seen typically if you're the strong type  a  personality usually your partner  isn't right because if you are both  strong type a personalities you're  always fighting  uh i you know i'm not the relationship  expert so i'm sure there's more  qualified people to talk about that but  but  you know i believe the person that  you're with your  life partner should be somebody who  supports  what you're doing and fits well with  your personality otherwise you're in  for a lifetime of fighting what i found  helps me in terms of the people so  you're asking about surrounding yourself  with people who  support you i have two groups of friends  and there's very little overlap between  them i have one group of friends that  are my entrepreneur friends  and and we meet up we talk about  business we're we're goal oriented we're  focused we're driven we're let's go  achieve this you know let's do something  great  and i have a group of i call mastermind  group we meet every  every month there's two groups and and  we sit down we push each other be better  be stronger do something amazing  uh rah-rah-rah you know like getting the  blood pumping  uh massive achievement that's your type  a  you know action right there and then i  have my other group of friends that are  salsa friends  and i'll spend like 20 hours a week in  the salsa community dancing djing  teaching sometimes uh and salsa people  are the exact opposite at least  here they're can i say lazier they're  lazier  they're not as responsible they  are more chill laid back don't show up  to things on time  which is the complete opposite of my  entrepreneur friends  and so i balance it you know  some weeks i'm spending a lot more time  doing salsa  when i just need a break i need to relax  i don't want to think about all the  craziness that that is the business  and i'll hang out with those people the  salsa people who  just you know just fun time uh and relax  and then you know if i'm feeling too  relaxed  and i need to go do something i need  some energy  i'll go hang out with my entrepreneur  friends and and we'll talk business and  we'll get excited and we'll help each  other's companies and we'll get new  things that we can  even if i'm talking about it i'm  speaking faster i'm more energetic  and so i think you need to balance those  out and  you know you have to find whatever ratio  works for you  you know the people you surround  yourself with you have a choice these  are your friends you have a choice of  who you hang out with  it sounds like you have a lot of the  people who are the chill laid back  kind of people so you have that covered  off you may want to find people who are  more ambitious  ready to go you know drive  drive our goal forward make things  happen kind of people  and you can either form your own group  or or look for an existing group to join  uh because getting that other group to  kind of motivate you and surround  yourself with will help you  cover off that side of your personality  and then when you're ready to chill and  relax you have your other friends to  help you out too  anyway that's what works for me  hopefully that helped you jacob great  question for those of you watching you  like the video  give it a thumbs up below let me know  what you think how do you handle that  question  how do you balance your work and your  leisure activities leave a comment  below you have a question for me leave  it below too i'll make a video response  just like this  and click on my face to subscribe to the  channel see more videos like this  thank you so much for watching i really  appreciate it and i'll see you soon  you
 

